olute error of the tem- perature reading?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"± 0.05 °C"},{"label":"B","text":"± 0.5 °C 3 Measurement, Errors and Data 38"},{"label":"C","text":"± 1.0 °C"},{"label":"D","text":"± 5.0 °C"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"2e89b6644007e17e8b55fb4494fda3f73465480e"},{"id":"q-c622ecd42cea","stem":"What does the standard deviation of the mean represent? For values that are normally distributed, it represents","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Biostatistics and Research","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the value above and below the mean that includes 68 % of all data values"},{"label":"B","text":"the difference between the highest data value and the lowest data value"},{"label":"C","text":"the average of the difference between each data value and the mean value."},{"label":"D","text":"the spread of the normal distribution."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Biostatistics and Research","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_w