n- dard deviation”?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a measure of central tendency."},{"label":"B","text":"It is only applicable to qualitative measurements."},{"label":"C","text":"Standard deviation is also known as the “variance”."},{"label":"D","text":"95 % of all data lie within two standard deviations of the mean."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"81c023f74dfe0f19223f70e6ca6061e346195d89"},{"id":"q-ac1e5dc02c7a","stem":"1 ml of water has a mass of 1.00 g. Which of the following sets of 3 measure- ments of the mass of 1 ml of water is the most precise set?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"0.98 g, 1.00 g, 1.02 g"},{"label":"B","text":"0.99 g, 0.99 g, 0.99 g"},{"label":"C","text":"1.00 g, 1.01 g, 1.02 g"},{"label":"D","text":"0.99 g, 0.99 g, 1.00 g"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGro