pH of more than 7 when in solution"},{"label":"D","text":"reacts with water to produce hydronium ions"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"fd382162282f8e634d9363ff1d7bb27ba3225f20"},{"id":"q-675c4920fc28","stem":"What effect would an acid have when added to the following solutions?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tap water: – it would react to produce hydronium ions."},{"label":"B","text":"Tap water: – it would react to produce hydroxide ions."},{"label":"C","text":"Buffered water: – it would lower the pH of the solution. 4 Chemistry for Physiology 91"},{"label":"D","text":"Un-buffered water: it would raise the pH of the solution."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"41c9bfb7b5366f2df504ce653c6d559cafd26fad"},{"id":"q-c8ca7a77e862","stem":"Choose the INCORRECT statement about buffer solutions.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Medical Biochemistry","topic":"Water, pH and Buffers","topicOriginal":"Water, pH and Buffers","subtopic":"Buffer","suggestedTopic":nu