d Coagulation","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hemostasis","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e08cedab6c86","stem":"A 35 year old O-negative male trauma patient receives a transfusion of two units of O-positive red blood cells before his blood type is known. After his typing is completed, he is switched to O-negative and he receives 6 additional type-specific RBC units. He survives and is transferred to the surgical ICU. Which of the following is TRUE regarding his situation?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Transfusion Medicine","topicOriginal":"Transfusion Medicine","subtopic":"Blood Grouping and Compatibility","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Transfusion Medicine","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-50ee99c81b55","stem":"In which of the following groups is Weak D testing required if the initial D typing results appear negative?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f1626dddfdb8","stem":"If a patient had a positive direct antiglobulin test (DAT) with Anti-IgG, what would happen if you performed a Weak D test on the patient cells?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1b93268ef0a5","stem":"What is the lowest acceptable hematocrit for female donors?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3de6813a1062","stem":"A smear that is prepared from equal parts of methylene blue and whole blood will be used for","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"WBC differential"},{"label":"B","text":"Platelet estimates"},{"label":"C","text":"Reticulocyte count"},{"label":"D","text":"RBC count"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e640a96e158a","stem":"What is the major cause of pernicious anemia?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Red Cell Di