 stage?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Malaria","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"trypomastigotes"},{"label":"B","text":"sporozoites"},{"label":"C","text":"gametocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"epimastigotes"},{"label":"E","text":"merozoites"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"provisional_independently_reasoned","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1eb487c7f0df","stem":"Secondary amebic abscesses are generally not lethal until they become established in what organ?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"small intestine"},{"label":"B","text":"lung"},{"label":"C","text":"brain"},{"label":"D","text":"liver"},{"label":"E","text":"cardiac muscle"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-af741d7836e9","stem":"Identify the true statement.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Entamoeba coli is rarely found in the continental U.S."},{"label":"B","text":"mature cysts of Entamoeba histolytica contain between 4 and 8 nuclei"},{"label":"C","text":"Entamoeba histolytica is the only intestinal amoebae of humans which routinely 