ogy","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-121d711d7d1d","stem":"Match the protozoan with the primary tissue/cells infected in the mammalian host. [50 points] ____ sexual stage of Toxoplasma gondi ____ cystic stage of Toxoplasma gondi ____ acute phase of Trypansoma cruzi ____ chronic phase of Trypansoma cruzi ____ acute phase of Trypanosoma brucei ____ chronic phase of Trypanosoma brucei ____ Giardia intestinalis ____ Naegleria fowleri ____ Isospora belli ____ Iodamoeba buetchlii ____ Cryptosporidium parvum ____ Trichomonas vaginalis ____ Entamoeba coli ____ Endolimax nana ____ Entamoeba histolytica ____ Trichomonas hominis ____ Plasmodium vivax ____ Acanthamoeba polyphagia ____ Trichomonas tenax ____ sexual stage of Saracocystis hominis ____ cystic stage of Saracocystis hominis ____ Iodamoeba buetschlii ____ Leishmania tropica ____ Entamoeba gingivalis ____ Leishmania donavani","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Malaria","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"any soft tissue"},{"label":"B","text":"blood fluid"},{"label":"C","text":"cardiac muscle"},{"label":"D","text":"intestinal lumen"},{"label":"E","text":"intestinal cells"},{"label":"F","text":"kidney"},{"label":"G","text":"liver"},{"label":"H","text":"nervous tissue I. lung J. oral cavity K. red blood cells L. skeletal muscle M. skin N. vaginal cavity"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-15488d5b1c82","stem":"Circle those parasites from the list below which are endemic to (currently being transmitted to humans in) South Dakota [18 points]","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cryptosporidium parvum"},{"label":"B","text":"Giardia intestinalis"},{"label":"C","text":"Plasmodium vivax"},{"label":"D","text":"Leishmania donavani"},{"label":"E","text":"Toxoplasma gondi"},{"label":"F","text":"Trichomonas tenax"},{"label":"G","text":"Trichomonas vaginalis"},{"label":"H","text":"Trypanosoma brucei rhodesience I. Trypansoma cruzi SDSU GENERAL PARASITOLGY: 467 LECTURE EXAM #2: OCTOBER 12, 2005 ESSAY PORTION NAME: ____________________"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-720f8e726e64","stem":"Describe why each of the following parasitic diseases are occasionally so difficult to diagnose with older conventional techniques (non-immunological). [12 points]","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6e7170b811ba","stem":"Why is malaria often referred to as “black water fever”? What causes this condition? (Hint: what cells does malaria damage, and what is the secondary effects of that damage?) [10 points]","type":"Short Answer","subject":"