orms are in the genus________________","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dipylidium"},{"label":"B","text":"Taenia"},{"label":"C","text":"Mesocestoides"},{"label":"D","text":"Diphyllobothrium"},{"label":"E","text":"Echinococcus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"607ff70b819120beee6b144453196c8dc7e79301"},{"id":"q-61a3e2ff4a2a","stem":"Which parasite from the list below is occasionally misdiagnosed in humans as a liver carcinoma?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fasciola hepatica"},{"label":"B","text":"Echinococcus granulosus"},{"label":"C","text":"Echinococcus multilocularis"},{"label":"D","text":"Taenia solium"},{"label":"E","text":"Paragonimus westermani"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-978f73ded2db","stem":"Swimmer's itch are caused by certain members of which family of parasite?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Troglotrematidae"},{"label":"B","text":"Dilepididae"},{"label":"C","text":"Fascioliae"},{"label":"D","text":"Taeniidae"},{"label":"E","text":"Schistosomatidae"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4bcc47b719fe8c5117df4872053bfa70972aaf1e"},{"id":"q-31dabf4441ef","stem":"Schistosomes evade the mammalian immune system primarily by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Schistosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the process of antigenic variation"},{"label":"B","text":"the effects of premunition"},{"label":"C","text":"masking itself with host antigens"},{"label":"D","text":"penetrating into priveleged sites within the body"},{"label":"E","text":"fast cars * FOR QUESTIONS ??-??, IDENTIFY THE HUMAN TISSUE INFECTED BY EACH OF THE FOLLOWING FLATWORMS. MARK THE LETTER : \"A\" IF THEY LIVE IN THE LUMEN OF THE INTESTINE, \"B\" IF THEY LIVE IN THE LIVER, \"C\" IF THEY LIVE IN THE LUNGS, \"D\" IF THEY LIVE IN MUSCLE OR SUBCUTANEOUS, \"E\" IF THEY LIVE IN A BLOOD VESSEL."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b80ca5cf43e0bb808de24ba528cbb140de0ec7a2"},{"id":"q-e32d3bc66125","stem":"Match each flatworms species with its life-cycle. You may use some of the answers more than once or not at all. (48 points) ____ Fasciola hepatica ____ Diphyllobothrium latum ____ Schistosoma japonicum ____ Clinorchis sinensis ____ Mesocestoides corti ____ Taenia solium ____ Schistosoma haematobium ____ Spirometra mansonoides ____ Taenia multiceps ____ Echinococcus granulosus ____ Paragonimus westermani ____ Dipylidium caninum ____ Schistosoma mansoni ____ Echinococcus multilocularis ____ Taenia saginata ____ Dicrocoelium dendriticum","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Schistosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"cysts ➩ adult ➩ cysts"},{"label":"B","text":"eggs ➩ adult ➩ eggs"},{"label":"C","text":"egg ➩ miracidia ➩ sporocyst and/or redia ➩ cercaria ➩ adult"},{"label":"D","text":"egg ➩ cercaria ➩ sporocyst and/or redia ➩ miracidium ➩ adult"},{"label":"E","text":"egg ➩ sporocyst and/or redia ➩ miracidium ➩ cercaria ➩ adult"},{"label":"F","text":"egg ➩ miracidia ➩ sporocyst and/or redia ➩ cercaria ➩ metacercaria ➩ adult"},{"label":"G","text":"egg ➩ hydatid cyst ➩ adult"},{"label":"H","text":"egg ➩ cysticercus ➩ adult I. egg ➩ coenurus ➩ adult J. egg ➩ plerocercoid ➩ procercoid ➩ adult K. egg ➩ procercoid ➩ plerocercoid ➩ adult L. egg ➩ cysticercoid ➩ adult M. egg ➩ adult ➩ egg N. egg ➩ cysticercoid ➩ tetrathyridium ➩ adult O. egg ➩ tetrathyridium ➩ cysticercoid ➩ adult ESSAY PORTION"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d8aa981efa86","stem":"Contrast current global distribution of Echinococcus multilocularis to that of Echinococcus granulosus (you can draw maps if you like). What intermediate host limits the distribution of E. granulosus?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f15a724e8785","stem":"As a result of littering in Custer State Park, Mother Nature has sentenced you to become infected with a helminth. She will allow you to pick your own \"poison\" from the list below. In order to minimize your penance (based on degree of pathology and ease of treatment) you should pick ________________________________.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Clinorchis sinensis"},{"label":"B","text":"Schistosoma japonicum"},{"label":"C","text":"Echinococcus granulosus"},{"label":"D","text":"Taenia saginata"},{"label":"E","text":"Paragonimus westermani"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bc1b86b6e119","stem":"The best method for preventing Echinococcus granulosus infections in dogs and cats includes minimizing","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"direct contact with other infected dogs and cats"},{"label":"B","text":"direct contact with infected humans"},{"label":"C","text":"consumption of infected rodents"},{"label":"D","text":"consumption of infected sheep"},{"label":"E","text":"mosquito bites"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-efb9ec1de8c8","stem":"Which parasite from the list below is least likely to be found in north central U.S.A.?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mesocestoides corti"},{"label":"B","text":"Echinococcus multilocularis"},{"label":"C","text":"Clinorchis sinensis"},{"label":"D","text":"Taenia saginata"},{"label":"E","text":"Diphyllobothrium latum"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0dc12a5adeac","stem":"Which parasite from the list below has been associated with the development of pernicious anemia, especially in individuals of Finnish descent?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Diphyllobothrium latum"},{"label":"B","text":"Echinococcus granulosus"},{"label":"C","text":"Spirometra mansonoides"},{"label":"D","text":"Schistosoma haematobium"},{"label":"E","text":"Paragonimus westermani"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-98dc0a0ed38f","stem":"In trematodes and cestodes, fertilization of the ovum takes place in which organ?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Cestodes","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"seminal vesicle"},{"label":"B","text":"Mehlis' gland"},{"label":"C","text":"vitellaria"},{"label":"D","text":"oviduct"},{"label":"E","text":"ovary"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3aa20584510b","stem":"Starting with the egg and ending with the adult, what is the correct order of development in the Pseudophyllidean life- cycle.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"egg ➩ plerocercoid ➩ procercoid ➩ adult"},{"label":"B","text":"egg ➩ coracidium ➩ cysticercoid ➩ adult"},{"label":"C","text":"egg ➩ cysticercoid ➩ adult"},{"label":"D","text":"egg ➩ procercoid ➩ cysticercoid ➩ adult"},{"label":"E","text":"egg ➩ coracidium ➩ procercoid ➩ plerocercoid ➩ adult"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d2a49d50dd86","stem":"Echincoccus granulosus would most likely be found in which country from the list below?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Argentina"},{"label":"B","text":"France"},{"label":"C","text":"Japan"},{"label":"D","text":"U.S."},{"label":"E","text":"Russia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ae6f9ade6815","stem":"Starting with the egg and ending with the adult, what is the correct order of development in the trematode life-cycle.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"egg ➩ miracidium ➩ cercaria ➩ redia ➩ sporocyst ➩ adult"},{"label":"B","text":"egg ➩ redia ➩ sporocyst ➩ cercaria ➩ miracidium ➩ adult"},{"label":"C","text":"egg ➩ miracidium ➩ sporocyst ➩ redia ➩ cercaria ➩ adult"},{"label":"D","text":"egg ➩ cercaria ➩ miracidium ➩ redia ➩ sporocyst ➩ adult"},{"label":"E","text":"egg ➩ cercaria ➩ sporocyst ➩ redia ➩ miracidium ➩ adult SDSU GENERAL PARASITOLGY: 467 LECTURE EXAM #3: NOVEMBER 9, 2005 MATCHING PORTION NAME: _______________________"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"de0bf2d4170e2abda8ea4bd7dc3673879d51a095"},{"id":"q-135244f36baa","stem":"Match the term below with the flatworm group that it is specific for; you must be as specific as possible, but do not be more specific than you can (i.e. if I had asked for strobila, you should respond with \"L\"; however, if I had asked for interproglottid gland, you should respond with \"J\"); you can use the answers more than once or not at all. Give the best answer for each (i.e. one answer only) [69 points] ____ acoelomate ____ beef tapeworm ____ calcareous corpuscle ____ cercaria ____ Chinese liver fluke ____ coenurus ____ coracidium ____ egg with terminal spine ____ fish tapeworm ____ hydatid cyst ____ lateral genital pore ____ lung fluke ____ oncosphere ____ neurocysticercosis ____ pork tapeworm ____ procercoid ____ protonephridia ____ protoscolex ____ rostellum ____ sparganum ____ striated egg shell ____ tegument ____ tetrathyridium","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Cestodes","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cestoda"},{"label":"B","text":"Clinorchis sinensis"},{"label":"C","text":"Cyclophyllidea"},{"label":"D","text":"Dicrocoelium dendriticum"},{"label":"E","text":"Diphyllobothrium latum"},{"label":"F","text":"Dipylidium caninus"},{"label":"G","text":"Echinococcus"},{"label":"H","text":"Echinococcus granulosus I Echinococcus multilocularis J. Fasciola hepatica K. Mesocestoididae L. Paragonimus westermani M. Platyhelminthes N. Pseudophyllidea O. Schistosomatidae P. Schistosoma Q. Schistosoma haematobium R. Schistosoma mansoni S. Spirometra mansonoides T. Taenia U. Taenia multiceps V. Taenia pisiformis W Taenia saginata X. Taenia solium Y. Taenia taeniaeformis Z. Taeniidae AA. Trematoda SDSU GENERAL PARASITOLGY: 467 LECTURE EXAM #3: NOVEMBER 9, 2005 ESSAY PORTION NAME: ____________________"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3b3ab7996652","stem":"List six different tapeworm genera that can parasitize either dogs or cats [12 points]. a. b. c. d. e. f. [pic][pic] Total Points: 190 Multiple Choice Points: 3 X 25 = 75 Matching Points: (3 X 20) + (7 X 3) = 81 Essay Points: 34 Close SDSU GENERAL PARASITOLOGY: 467 LECTURE EXAM #3: NOVEMBER 9, 2005 NAME: _______________________ For questions 1-25, choose the best answer; if all of the answers are correct, you must choose that option. [2 points each]","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Cestodes","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cce1e75b198b","stem":"List six different tapeworm genera that can parasitize either dogs or cats [12 points]. a. b. c. d. e. f. Parasitology Exam Nematodes I. Identify (20 points)","type":"Image / Diagram Question","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Cestodes","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-55fd4483a0cb","stem":"A cashier at a small grocery store in South Carolina frequented by migrant farm workers has developed a serious bronchial condition. The pulmonary condition passes but shortly thereafter a rash develops and the individual is unable to sleep. What organism would you suspect has caused this and how would you validate your suspicions?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3a4f0852b32d","stem":"A Tourist visiting southern China feels stifled by the restriction place upon him by the tour guide and to rectify the situation and improve the enjoyment of his trip, he befriends a native and is invited to dinner at his rural home. The meal is different by western standards and includes amongst other things, unshelled water chestnuts, raw fish and fried rice. Upon returning within two week to the US, he develops a severe, chronic headache, coupled with intestinal discomfort. Upon seeing a number of physicians, he discovers there are two different helminth ova in his stool. What organisms were likely encountered and how would you identify them?","type":"Image / Diagram Question","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2c76af7de71c","stem":"A young married couple decide to celebrate a newly-discovered pregnancy. Friends invited them to a Texas-style barbecue in which pork and beef were served. Within a few days, the wife developed symptoms of the flu but quickly recovered. The pregnancy was uneventful but the baby developed severe neurological problems and became profoundly mentally handicapped. Explain the scenario and the organism involved. III. Diagram the life cycle of Ascaris lumbricoides. What about the life cycle suggests that Ascaris may have evolved from a nematode which invades its host by penetrating the skin?","type":"Image / Diagram Question","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-657f92c09916","stem":"Explain what you understand by the term \"critical hatching conditions\" and its significance in the epidemiology of nematode infections in UK. [Answer]","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Measures and Study Designs","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated",