 were set from December 1995 onwards as part of the General pathology I & II courses and will give you an idea of the kind of questions that will be set for the Infection & Immunity course from 2003 onwards.","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-295dbe9982dd","stem":"Describe the role of Toxoplasma gondii as a cause of abortion in sheep","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-afda92e93b6f","stem":"How does the knowledge of the life cycle of a nematode lead to effective control?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-985c37be88ab","stem":"Discuss the factors that influence the maintenance of enzootic stability of Babesia divergens in the UK.","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9d0f11d31ac2","stem":"Explain what is meant by the term myiasis and differentiate between facultative myiasis and obligate myiasis. Briefly describe the life cycle and clinical consequences of one example of each of these two types of myiasis to illustrate your answer.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8dfda4afaa0f","stem":"Describe the important pathological features of nematode migration within the final host. Use named examples to illustrate your answers.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f1c4ab69e84e","stem":"Compare and contrast the routes and mechanisms by which pathogens are transmitted by ticks, and pathogens transmitted by insects, get from one mammal host to another. In your answer use one named example of a pathogen transmitted by a tick, and one transmitted by an insect.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c43ed66e2d49","stem":"Describe the epidemiological significance of environmentally-related adaptations to the life-cycle of trichostrongyle nematodes in temperate countries. Illustrate your answer by reference to appropriate named parasites.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Measures and Study Designs","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-53222fec1103","stem":"Describe briefly the life-cycle of the sheep tick Ixodes ricinus and exhaling how the life-cycle and feeding behavior results in transmission of a tick-borne pathogen of your choice. [pic] BIOLOGY 545 LECTURE EXAM Trematodes and Cestodes (100 PTS) NOTE: A species is binomial; do not abbreviate generic names.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","subject_suggestion_available"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_suggestion_available","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-18ce0e433314","stem":"The following represents some key characteristics or key words describing some of the parasites. Please write in the correct species of worm behind the prompt. More than one parasite may pertain to a particular question, but please just give one answer. In addition, some parasites may be used more than once (2 point each, 20 points total).","type":"Multiple Response","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sparganosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Large lateral spine on egg"},{"label":"C","text":"Unilocular hydatid cyst"},{"label":"D","text":"Adults in lungs"},{"label":"E","text":"Cephalic cone"},{"label":"F","text":"Mesocercariae"},{"label":"G","text":"Salmon poisoning"},{"label":"H","text":"Measly beef I. Polar filament J. Slime balls"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dcca0d5c6496","stem":"Please define each of the following terms in one sentence or less. Please be sure to give a species of trematode or cestode representative of each (2 points each, 22 points total).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dioecious"},{"label":"B","text":"Gynecophoral canal"},{"label":"C","text":"Bothria"},{"label":"D","text":"Coracidium"},{"label":"E","text":"Acetabulum"},{"label":"F","text":"Redia"},{"label":"G","text":"Rostellum"},{"label":"H","text":"Procercoid I. Metacercariae J. Miracidium K. Egg packets"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ad76b003281b","stem":"Name a commonly used drug for treating many trematode and cestode infections in humans (2 points).","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c5420c12dd97","stem":"Please compare and contrast the following terms (i.e. give a similarity between the two, and give a difference between the two). Be sure to give a representative species for each term (4 point each, 12 points total).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Redia versus Sporocyst"},{"label":"B","text":"Cysticercoid versus Cysticercus"},{"label":"C","text":"Metacercaria versus Mesocercaria"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3ec6b9185d43","stem":"If you were provided an intact adult tapeworm and were asked whether it was Taenia solium or Taenia saginatus, what would be the 2 most important criteria that you would use to distinguish between the two species?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Cestodes","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3e2beb3b5e7e","stem":"Provide the appropriate species (2 points each; 40 points total). In a few cases, more than one species of worm may apply, but just give one answer. Also, a species of worm may be used more than once.","type":"Multiple Response","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Transmitted by blackflies."},{"label":"B","text":"Finger clubbing."},{"label":"C","text":"Pica."},{"label":"D","text":"Egg flattened on one side."},{"label":"E","text":"Bipolar plugs on eggs."},{"label":"F","text":"Calcified larvae in skeletal muscle."},{"label":"G","text":"River blindness."},{"label":"H","text":"Sushi. I. Adults in subcutaneous nodules. J. Rhabditiform larvae in feces. K. Eggs in urine. L. Common in raccoon intestine. M. Calabar swellings. N. Serpent on a staff. O. Parthenogenic females. P. Chyluria. Q. Eggs in liver tissue. R. Prolapsed rectum. S. Elephantiasis below the waist. T. Heartworm."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3995fea65d42","stem":"Name a drug useful for treating many intestinal nematode infections (2 points).","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ee95440c810d","stem":"Please write in the name of an appropriate species. Some questions may have more than one answer, but please just give 1 representative species. You may use an answer more than once (2 points each; 30 points total).","type":"Multiple Response","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Amoeba cysts with 8-16 nuclei."},{"label":"B","text":"60% binucleate amoebic trophozoites."},{"label":"C","text":"Duffy antigen."},{"label":"D","text":"2 sporocysts in oocyst."},{"label":"E","text":"8 merozoites average in segmenter."},{"label":"F","text":"Variable surface glycoproteins."},{"label":"G","text":"A relapsing malaria."},{"label":"H","text":"Always infects lungs. I. RNA editing. J. Infects the urogenital tract. K. Macronucleus. L. Large glycogen vacuole in cyst. M. Blackwater fever. N. Hepatic abcesses. O. Only invades reticulocytes."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c16938cd052a","stem":"Please provide the common name of the intermediate host (IH), definitive host (D), or vector (V) for each of the following protozoa (2 points each, 10 points total).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sarcocystis hominis IH"},{"label":"B","text":"Toxoplasma gondii D"},{"label":"C","text":"Leishmania donovani V"},{"label":"D","text":"Isospora belli D"},{"label":"E","text":"Babesia bigemina V"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3154ff8b060d","stem":"Please provide the site of infection for each of the following protozoa (2 points each, 10 points total).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Naegleria fowleri"},{"label":"B","text":"Giardia lamblia"},{"label":"C","text":"Cryptosporidium parvum"},{"label":"D","text":"Balantidium coli"},{"label":"E","text":"Plasmodium ovale"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e455291c04a0","stem":"True or false (1 point each, 10 points total).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Plasmodium vivax occasionally exists in the United States."},{"label":"B","text":"Plasmodium falciparum only invades reticulocytes."},{"label":"C","text":"Toxoplasma gondii is a significant pathogen of AIDS patients."},{"label":"D","text":"Entamoeba histolytica grows well at room temperature and with high oxygen."},{"label":"E","text":"Penicillin is highly effective at eliminating Naegleria fowleri."},{"label":"F","text":"In addition to humans, Balantidium coli also infects pigs."},{"label":"G","text":"Trypanosoma cruzi causes significant morbidity and mortality in populations along the lower Rio Grande valley in Texas."},{"label":"H","text":"The primary vectors of Leishmania in Oklahoma and Texas are reduviids. I. Home made saline solutions are highly effective in eliminating Acanthamoeba spp. trophozoites. J. Cryptosporidium parvum is easily eliminated with metronidazole."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b20675724321","stem":"Provide the name of the species (or in some cases genus or common name) of a parasite associated with each of the following (2 pts each, 40 points total). If more than one answer applies, just give one answer. An answer may be used more than once.","type":"Multiple Response","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Possesses a proboscis with hooks (common name only)."},{"label":"B","text":"Soft tick that is sometimes found in the ear."},{"label":"C","text":"A species of flea where the female burrows into skin."},{"label":"D","text":"Maggots that suck blood."},{"label":"E","text":"Body louse."},{"label":"F","text":"Crab louse."},{"label":"G","text":"Transmits Lyme disease."},{"label":"H","text":"Both genal and pronotal combs. I. Lone star tick. J. an arthropod that lives in hair follicles. K. Lays eggs in wounds. L. Primary screwworm. M. Genus of tick with no festoons. N. Fly that gives birth to live larvae (genus only). O. American dog tick. P. Human botfly. Q. Bedbug. R. Blackfly (genus only). S. Tsetse fly (genus only). T. Sandfly (genus only)."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-265247fcbaef","stem":"Below are a list of diseases/parasites. Please provide the name of a species of arthropod, pentastome, leech, or acanthocephalan associated with that disease (2 pts each; 20 points total).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Trypanosoma cruzi (common name)."},{"label":"B","text":"Leishmaniasis (genus only)"},{"label":"C","text":"Plasmodium falciparum (genus only)."},{"label":"D","text":"Onchocerca volvulus (genus only)."},{"label":"E","text":"Bubonic plague."},{"label":"F","text":"Loa loa (genus only)."},{"label":"G","text":"7-year itch."},{"label":"H","text":"Dipylidium caninum. I. Lyme disease. J. Babesia spp."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"p